@prefix : <#> .
@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<> a schema:CreativeWork ;
    schema:name "howto/ub-isql-credential-resolution.ttl"@en ;
    schema:description "Resolution chain for the kidehen SQL/WebDAV account password used against UB: macOS Keychain item uriburner-isql / account kidehen (LIVE as of 2026-08-25, migrated from /tmp/uyi UB_PWD with the user's permission), /tmp/uyi UB_PWD=... was the migration SOURCE and was DELETED by the user's instruction on 2026-08-25 immediately after readback verification, so the Keychain is now the SOLE source. Third independent secret alongside p12-passphrase-retrieval.ttl (uriburner-p12) and virtuoso-local-dba-passphrase-retrieval.ttl (virtuoso-local-dba) — three DISTINCT keychain items, never shared or overloaded. Also records the verified transport topology: isql reaches this account only on localhost:1111, while WebDAV authenticates both locally and against linkeddata.uriburner.com."@en ;
    schema:dateCreated "2026-08-25T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema:author <https://linkedin.com/in/kidehen#this> ;
    schema:about :howto .

:howto a schema:HowTo ;
    schema:name "Resolve the kidehen UB password — Keychain first, /tmp/uyi fallback — and reach the right endpoint"@en ;
    schema:description "Procedure for authenticating isql sessions and WebDAV requests as the kidehen account without hardcoding or re-eliciting the password each session, plus the endpoint topology established by testing on 2026-08-25."@en ;
    schema:step :step-keychainItem, :step-canonicalSnippet, :step-endpointTopology, :step-connectFailVsBadLogin, :step-redact ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <p12-passphrase-retrieval.ttl>,
        <virtuoso-local-dba-passphrase-retrieval.ttl>,
        <credential-location-session-start.ttl>,
        <../core.ttl> .

:step-keychainItem a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:name "Keychain item uriburner-isql / account kidehen — a THIRD distinct item, never overloaded onto uriburner-p12 or virtuoso-local-dba"@en ;
    schema:text """CREATE (interactive form, value never passes through the agent):
  security add-generic-password -U -s uriburner-isql -a kidehen -T /usr/bin/security -w

READ:
  security find-generic-password -s uriburner-isql -a kidehen -w

NAMING NOTE: unlike the two sibling items, the account is the literal SQL username "kidehen", not "$USER". They happen to be the same string on this host, but the account field here denotes WHICH SQL login the secret unlocks, per the service-is-namespace / account-is-label convention in p12-passphrase-retrieval.ttl :step-storeCreation.

MIGRATED 2026-08-25: value copied from /tmp/uyi (single line, UB_PWD=..., 10 characters) into this new item by the agent, since the user explicitly asked for the same Keychain treatment already given to the p12 passphrase and the dba password, and the value was already resolvable from the documented /tmp/uyi fallback. Ordering followed :step-migrateExistingPlaintextSecret — VERIFY FREE (plain attribute read returned "could not be found", so no -U over an item of unknown provenance), then ADD, then VERIFY READBACK (string-compared against the source in-shell, printed only a match/mismatch boolean and the length, never the value). -T /usr/bin/security was supplied, and the readback confirmed non-interactive reads return the value with no GUI dialog."""@en .

:step-canonicalSnippet a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:name "Canonical fallback-safe snippets for isql and for WebDAV"@en ;
    schema:text """RESOLVE (Keychain is the SOLE source as of 2026-08-25 — /tmp/uyi was deleted, so the historical python3 fallback branch is dead and must NOT be reinstated):
  export UB_PWD="$(security find-generic-password -s uriburner-isql -a kidehen -w)"
If this returns empty, STOP and elicit from the user. Do not invent a fallback path.

ISQL:
  isql localhost:1111 kidehen "$UB_PWD" exec="..."
  unset UB_PWD

WEBDAV — pass the credential through a curl config file on stdin (curl -K -) rather than --user, so the value never appears in the process argument list where `ps` can read it:
  printf 'user = "kidehen:%s"\\n' "$UB_PWD" | curl -K - -X PROPFIND -H "Depth: 1" https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/DAV/home/kidehen/
  unset UB_PWD

Always unset immediately after the call. Never echo, never pass on a logged command line, never write into RDF memory or the transcript."""@en .

:step-endpointTopology a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:name "VERIFIED 2026-08-25: isql only on localhost:1111; WebDAV works local AND remote; remote SQL ports are firewalled"@en ;
    schema:text """Four paths tested end-to-end with the Keychain-sourced value, all succeeding:
  isql localhost:1111 as kidehen            -> select now(), user returned "kidehen"
  PROPFIND https://localhost/DAV/home/kidehen/            -> HTTP 207
  PROPFIND http://localhost:8890/DAV/home/kidehen/        -> HTTP 207
  PROPFIND https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/DAV/home/kidehen/ -> HTTP 207

REMOTE SQL IS NOT REACHABLE from this host. A TCP probe of linkeddata.uriburner.com found 1111 and 1112 closed/filtered and only 1113 open; 1113 is the TLS SQL listener documented in weblog-from-webdav/references/isql-mode.md, which expects an EMPTY SQL username with certificate/WebID authentication (-X p12, -T ca bundle) — a different credential entirely, not this password. So: use localhost:1111 for SQL as kidehen, and reserve the remote host for WebDAV over HTTPS."""@en .

:step-connectFailVsBadLogin a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:name "Distinguish VD CL033 (connect failed) from VD CL034 (bad login) BEFORE counting an attempt against the lockout budget"@en ;
    schema:text """The one-attempt-only discipline in virtuoso-local-dba-passphrase-retrieval.ttl :step-verificationFailed exists because repeated failed logins risk a Virtuoso account lockout. That budget is only consumed by an AUTHENTICATION failure:
  VD CL034: Bad login        -> the server rejected the credential. COUNTS. Stop; do not retry.
  VD CL033: Connect failed   -> no TCP/protocol session was ever established. DOES NOT COUNT. Safe to try another host/port.

On 2026-08-25 both remote isql attempts (1113, then 1111) returned CL033, so trying a third endpoint (localhost:1111) was safe and consumed no attempt. Read the error code before deciding whether you are allowed another try — treating CL033 as a failed login would have wrongly blocked the successful path, and treating CL034 as retryable would risk the lockout."""@en .

:step-redact a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:name "Never store the kidehen password in RDF memory, reports, or chat"@en ;
    schema:text "Record only WHICH source resolved it and whether the connection succeeded. Never copy the value into preferences.ttl, session TTL, howto files, commit messages, or chat. Reporting its character length or a match/mismatch boolean during verification is acceptable; reporting any part of the value is not."@en .
